# Generated adapter output — build artifacts, never committed
# `dist/*`, NOT `dist/` — git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so `dist/` made the negations below dead letters and every new file under
# dist/plugin was silently unstageable. Measured: `git check-ignore` reported
# `dist/plugin/skills/probe.md` ignored by this line while the tracked files beside it were
# fine, because a tracked file ignores .gitignore. Shipping the round table added
# dist/plugin/review/ and CI caught it as a stale dist that could not be committed.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead lets the exception apply.
dist/*
# Exception: the synthesized public plugin artifact IS distributed — the marketplace
# git-subdir source resolves it from dist/plugin, so the release flow commits it (WO 90a13043).
!dist/plugin/
!dist/plugin/**
skills/**/.planning/

