# Test/diagnostic output captures — write to ~/.dream-studio/diagnostics/ instead
#
# ANCHORED TO THE REPO ROOT, and that leading slash is the whole point. These patterns
# describe files a diagnostic run drops in the working directory. Unanchored, git applies
# them at EVERY depth, so they also match source whose name happens to start the same way
# — and the failure is silent, because an ignored file is simply never offered for commit.
#
# Measured: `lint-*` swallowed
# canonical/skills/domains/modes/website/scripts/lint-artifact.py, which fourteen
# instructions across the website skills tell an agent to run, one of them a severity:
# critical gotcha reading "before every delivery". It was never tracked once. Only a
# .pyc dated 2026-05-23 proved it had ever existed. `verify_*.py` did the same thing to
# nine product modules and needed the explicit un-ignore below to undo it.
/pytest-*
/diag-test-*
/smoke-*
/black-*
/lint-*
/drift-*

# Debug scripts (one-off investigations) — anchored for the same reason.
/tmp_*.py
/verify_*.py
tools/_ta*.md
tools/_ta*.py

# PR body drafts
pr-body-*.md

